      "id": "disabled-agent-weather",
      "category": "disabled_agent",
      "prompt": "What's the weather in Lexington right now?",
      "excluded_agents": [
        "weather-1"
      ],
      "accepted_agents": [
        "no_tool_needed",
        "general-1",
        "web-research-1"
      ],
      "accepted_tools": [
        "web-research-1__web_search",
        "general-1__search_wikipedia"
      ],
      "expected_tier": "high",
      "expected_style": "conversational",
      "note": "A disabled agent must never be offered, which is the assertion that matters. What the router does instead is a judgement call: searching the web for the weather when the weather agent is unavailable is useful, not a routing error. The first version of this label accepted only no_tool_needed and was measuring label strictness rather than router quality. Widened 2026-09-17 after a live run routed it to web search at 0.87/0.97 confidence."
    },
